  "question": {
    "text": "Four fair dice are thrown independently 27 times. Then the expected number of times, at least two dice show up a three or a five, is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>There are only two outcomes, success which stands for getting either 3 or 5, and failure, stands for getting any other outcome.</p><p>Probability for success<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Probability for failure<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Number of trials<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p><p>Number of dice<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Using Binomial Probability,</p><p>P(at least 2 shows 3 or 5)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>384</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Expectation is numerically same as mean.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> expectation<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p>"
  }
